	<section_number>46.2-810</section_number>
	<catch_line>Age limits for drivers of public passenger-carrying vehicles</catch_line>
	<text>
		No person, whether licensed or not, under the age of eighteen years shall drive a motor vehicle while in use as a public passenger-carrying vehicle.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 46-182; 1958, c. 541, § 46.1-170; 1970, c. 481; 1972, cc. 386, 823; 1989, c. 727.</history>
